{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"bdd03d82d04cb34632011fc6bc884cb7e7f345dc0cc7d19d820fdd92b81b8b8d","packTokens":2466,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"side","tokens":100,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":79,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":880,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":1301,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"PRODUCT SIDE. This run builds the API side of the product these requirements describe, in an existing .NET API project: every operation of the locked API contract in contracts/openapi.yaml, exactly as it is written there, and the data behind them. The web app is built in its own repo: no screen is built here, and no criterion is written for one.\n\nMap each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Build the API side in the existing .NET API project.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Implement every operation in contracts/openapi.yaml exactly as written.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Implement the data behind the API operations.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"Should the backend persist and execute the broader product workflows only when an operation in the locked OpenAPI contract exposes them, or should it also build data/workflows for capabilities that the contract does not expose?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Implement the data and business rules needed by contracted operations only; do not add uncontracted API operations.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"For contracted operations, should access enforcement include the detailed warehouse, organisation, and role restrictions described in the user stories, beyond whatever security is declared in the OpenAPI contract?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Enforce the user stories' explicit restrictions on contracted data: customer-organisation isolation, warehouse assignments, staff roles, and Auditor read-only access, without changing the API surface.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"Where the contracted receipt operations expose stock receipt behavior, which of the narrative receipt and quality rules must the API enforce and persist?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Apply the explicit receipt rules where exposed: separate traceable receipt records even for repeated product/lot pairs, quarantine on receipt, Quality Officer release, and the stated expiry restrictions.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"For contracted customer-order and allocation operations, how much of the described order lifecycle should be implemented beyond basic persistence of contract fields?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Apply the explicit order rules where exposed: customer changes/cancellation only before packing, duplicate-submission protection, suitable-stock allocation, and the stated allocation and back-order behavior.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"How broad should the audit history be for contracted data changes? The request requires an audit trail and says records can be changed after the fact, but does not define the complete event set or immutability behavior.\",\n  \"answer\": \"Store actor and time for consequential changes and decisions exposed by contracted operations.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"How long must audit events for consequential changes and decisions remain available?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Retain audit events without automatic expiry.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"What should happen to the existing spreadsheet-based operational data when the API is introduced?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Do not migrate legacy data; start with records entered through the contracted API operations.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"When the configured database is unavailable or invalid, what should the API do beyond the existing fail-fast behavior for a missing connection string?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Fail startup for invalid configuration and return the contract-defined server error for failed operations; never report a business operation as successful.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Implement every operation and its methods, paths, parameters, headers, request and response schemas, media types, and statuses exactly as defined in `contracts/openapi.yaml`, without adding uncontracted business operations.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Implement the locked API contract under the `/api` prefix while preserving the existing root health response, OpenAPI document, and Swagger UI.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Persist contracted records, relationships, state changes, and file artifacts in the configured shared database; retain successful mutations across restarts and do not import legacy spreadsheet or paper-process business data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Implement contracted staff authorization-URL lookup, customer email-and-password sign-in with one-time-code verification and resend, and password-reset request, token-inspection, and completion flows, delivering customer codes and reset links by email.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Enforce contracted customer-organisation, staff-role, warehouse-scope, Auditor read-only, and account-status restrictions on every operation, including denial of access to deactivated accounts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Persist searchable products and immutable versioned temperature profiles, require a profile for each product, and validate profile tiers and governance history.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Persist separate contracted receipt, receipt-logger, receipt-evidence, stock, movement, and opening-stock records, and enforce receipt traceability, quarantine, expiry validation, and Quality Officer release.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Automatically mark expired handling units Expired, remove them from allocations, record the change, and alert the dispatcher through the contracted scheduled check.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Persist customer orders and dispatch allocations using the serving warehouse’s configured cut-off, working-day, holiday, time-zone, and customer shelf-life rules, and enforce idempotency, order validation, pre-packing customer changes, and cancellation rules.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Allocate only released, physically available stock meeting customer minimum remaining shelf life; select earliest expiry first with the specified stability-budget tie-break; and apply complete-order, partial-order, back-order, and override rules.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Persist compatible box packing and route plans, enforce box and route qualification, and record driver loading, departure, synchronization, handover, refusal, and delivery-evidence operations.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"Expose temperature histories for contracted entity types and persist available logger readings, gaps, excursions, tier-by-tier handling-unit budgets, related holds, and corrected history when readings arrive late or out of order.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"Persist quality cases, signed proposals and decisions, superseding decisions, and destruction records, applying the required two-person quality approval and decision-history rules.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"Persist signed recalls, trace selected lots through affected stock and delivery records, block affected stock still held, and record customer responses and signed closure or write-off decisions until quantities are accounted for.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"Implement customer organisation account, address, team, delivery, certificate, recall-notice, order, and language-preference operations with returned records and mutations scoped to the authenticated organisation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"Implement contracted administration, operational-report, and lot-history operations, persisting organisation shelf-life settings, account role and warehouse assignments, and chronological business records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"Record the actor and timestamp for consequential contracted changes and decisions in read-only audit events, and retain those events without automatic expiry.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"Fail startup if persistent-storage configuration is invalid; if storage is unavailable during a contracted operation, return the contract-defined server-error response without reporting the operation as successful.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"Send excursion alerts through the configured email channel to the driver when applicable, dispatcher, and warehouse Quality Officers after the triggering reading is received.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"Support logger and cold-room readings from concurrently reporting devices.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}